# MANDATORY: TRANSOVO Security & Authentication UX Standards (Guide #9)

**Scope:** All repository work — pages, APIs, `src/lib/`, jobs, and any customer-facing behavior. Read the full source doc before implementing.

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-SECURITY-AUTHENTICATION-STANDARDS.md`

## Hard requirement

Auth flows, session handling, permission checks, API routes, and sensitive actions **MUST** follow this guide. Read before touching login, settings security, middleware, or role-based UI **or** server handlers.

## Non-negotiables

### Always (UI + backend)
- **Server enforces authorization** — UI hiding is not security. Every `src/app/api/**` route must verify workspace/session/role.
- Sensitive actions require **appropriate confirmation** and audit trail where specified.
- Session expiry, re-auth, and lockout UX follow guide — no cryptic errors.
- **Never expose** secrets, tokens, or internal IDs in UI copy or API responses unnecessarily.
- Permission-denied states explain **what's missing**, not generic "Error".
- 2FA/MFA flows preserve context; recovery paths are documented in full doc.
- Admin/impersonation flows (if any) follow elevated-auth patterns in full doc.

### API / lib
- **Tenant isolation** — workspaceId scoping on every query and mutation.
- No auth bypass in dev paths shipped to production.
- Rate-limit and validate auth on webhooks per guide.

## On conflict

Security UX requirements beat convenience shortcuts.
